diff --git a/docs/ops/mail.md b/docs/ops/mail.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1dcbec2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/mail.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Account e-mails
+
+Account e-mails are rendered by Laravel's own notifications
+(`Illuminate\Auth\Notifications\ResetPassword` and `VerifyEmail`) in Brazilian
+Portuguese, with the PegaFila brand.
+
+## Locale and identity
+
+| Setting | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `APP_NAME` | `PegaFila` |
+| `APP_LOCALE` | `pt_BR` |
+| `APP_FALLBACK_LOCALE` | `en` |
+
+The same values are pinned in `phpunit.xml`, and the notification subjects live
+in `lang/pt_BR.json` (`"Reset your password"`, `"Verify your email address"`).
+Other strings (greeting, button, body, sub-copy) reuse Laravel's translated
+JSON entries, so no English footer/sub-copy leaks into pt-BR mail.
+
+## Mail theme
+
+Markdown mail uses the custom `pegafila` theme
+(`resources/views/vendor/mail/html/themes/pegafila.css`), selected through
+`config('mail.markdown.theme')`. The brand primary color `#0f7490` is applied to
+the action button, which is present in every account e-mail and survives CSS
+inlining.
+
+## Password reset flow (guests)
+
+| Route name | Method / URI | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `password.request` | `GET /forgot-password` | E-mail form |
+| `password.email` | `POST /forgot-password` | Validates e-mail, `throttle:6,1`, always flashes `passwords.sent` |
+| `password.reset` | `GET /reset-password/{token}` | New-password form |
+| `password.update` | `POST /reset-password` | Validates token/e-mail/password, rotates `remember_token`, fires `PasswordReset`, redirects to `/` |
+
+The request endpoint sends `ResetPassword` only when the address belongs to a
+user, but returns the same response either way so it never reveals whether an
+account exists. Passwords must be at least 8 characters with letters, mixed
+case and numbers, and must be confirmed.
+
+## Verification link
+
+`verification.verify` (`GET /email/verify/{id}/{hash}`) is protected by `auth`,
+`signed` and `throttle:6,1`. The `VerifyEmail` notification builds its URL from
+that named route; the controller marks the logged-in user as verified only when
+both the id and the hash match (403 otherwise) and then redirects to `/`.
+
+Guest handling of `auth` routes (login redirect) arrives with the login task.
